blurb: The South Portland Board of Education held its first FY26 budget workshop,
  grappling with the dual challenges of declining student enrollment and a significant
  property tax burden on residents. The superintendent presented a budget featuring
  over $3 million in staff and program reductions, sparking intense debate and public
  comment over cuts to curriculum leadership, social-emotional learning, and music
  programs.
